  "description": "Use common present-tense verbs to say what you speak, have, and like.",
  "grammar_note": "Regular -are verbs use -o for io (parlo), -i for tu (parli), and -a for lui/lei (parla). Avere is irregular: ho, hai, ha. Non comes before the verb to make a sentence negative: Non parlo inglese.",
